# Ordering direction shortcuts

Start with only ascending name enabled and alpha selected. All three discovered
sessions fit without scrolling. In ordering mode, Up and Down change the selected
comparator, not the selected session; the selected alpha follows its new row.

    :b jj tmux cat (available)
    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :t new-session -d -s alpha cat (success)
    :t new-session -d -s beta cat (success)
    :t resize-window -t runner:0 -x 100 -y 14 (success)
    :t respawn-pane -k -t runner:0 'smth --order "+name"; cat' (success)
    :p runner:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :k C-p C-s
    :snap --color

```terminal
session:                                                                                           ┃
  3/3 | [C-s] ◂ ↓name ▸ live · recency · attention   | [C-r] repo: none                            ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
▌■ alpha                                                                                           ┃
 ■ beta                                                                                            ┃
 ■ runner                                                                                          ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                  sort [C-g] cancel┃
```

![light](session-ordering-arrows.md.snap.1.light.svg)
![dark](session-ordering-arrows.md.snap.1.dark.svg)

Up switches directly from ascending to descending, displaying ↑name and moving
alpha below runner and beta. Repeating Up disables name, restoring discovery
order; pressing Up again enables descending. The other comparators stay disabled.

    :k up
    :snap --color

```terminal
session:                                                                                           ┃
  3/3 | [C-s] ◂ ↑name ▸ live · recency · attention   | [C-r] repo: none                            ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
 ■ runner                                                                                          ┃
 ■ beta                                                                                            ┃
▌■ alpha                                                                                           ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                  sort [C-g] cancel┃
```

